; The child's half.  Its apex NS RRset names ns-child.example., which is
; not the name the parent's referral gave, and gives it an address.
;
; So the two NS RRsets have nothing in common but the zone they are
; about.  Both names lead to this same server, so neither set is wrong
; about where the zone is -- the disagreement is in the names alone.
; www.diffns.internot.jp is this, and BIND is said to answer SERVFAIL
; for it.
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 3600
@		IN	SOA	ns-child.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@		IN	NS	ns-child.example.
ns-child	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
www		IN	A	192.0.2.2
